  "notes": [
    {
      "note_id": "D0",
      "type": "source",
      "text": "Definition agreed in discussion with Juan Vaz and Fahim Ebrahimi, 2026-11-18."
    },
    {
      "note_id": "D1",
      "type": "source",
      "text": "The Cause of Death Register uses the international ICD-9, so 155A (liver cancer) is recorded as 155.0 (or most often 1550). ICD-9 codes in this list are therefore written in the international format."
    },
    {
      "note_id": "D2",
      "type": "source",
      "text": "In a sensitivity analysis, consider also using secondary causes of death with a liver-related diagnosis."
    },
    {
      "note_id": "D3",
      "type": "source",
      "text": "Liver-related death is also a component of MALO."
    },
    {
      "note_id": "D4",
      "type": "source",
      "text": "Not included: secondary liver tumours (ICD-10 C78.7), gallbladder and bile duct disease (K80-K82, K83.1-K83.9), and jaundice and hepatomegaly as symptoms (R16, R17)."
    },
    {
      "note_id": "D5",
      "type": "source",
      "text": "Metabolic liver disease is optional (variant \"optional\"); the source lists no ICD-7 code for it."
    },
    {
      "note_id": "D6",
      "type": "source",
      "text": "ICD-10 K83.0 is described in the source as cholangitis, including sclerosing cholangitis (PSC)."
    },
    {
      "note_id": "D7",
      "type": "curator",
      "text": "Ranges are written as in the source: the three-digit ICD-8 and ICD-9 categories 570-573 and the ICD-10 range K70-K77 stand for the whole category. ICD-10 K75, K76 and K77 appear in the source after a semicolon."
    },
    {
      "note_id": "D8",
      "type": "curator",
      "text": "The source table has two empty sub-rows (\"Cirrhosis, fibrosis, biliary cirrhosis\" and \"Liver failure, hepatitis and other liver disease\") under the alcoholic/toxic row, with no codes entered. They are not represented here."
    },
    {
      "note_id": "D9",
      "type": "curator",
      "text": "ICD-8 571,90 is cirrhosis with portal hypertension, ICD-8 573,02 hepatic coma, ICD-8 785,30 ascites (the same ICD-8 ascites code as in the MALO list)."
    }
  ]
}